From 3db4b79971ea1add5637ef23e49c799d94c5a49d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:03:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telegram): inbox notifications in the member's DM;
 decision buttons

A member who bound a Telegram bot gets every new inbox item in that bot's
DM, like the WeCom smart bot's inbox push: what they mute in Multica's
notification settings never becomes an item, so it is not sent either. The
bot of the agent behind the item is preferred
(FindChannelBindingForMemberOnAgentInstallation), else the member's newest
binding. A mention carries its comment text.

A new decision (patch 0008) now raises an inbox item "decision_requested"
(action required) for the issue's member subscribers, else the workspace's
owners and admins. In Telegram it carries one button per option; a press by
the bound member answers the decision and posts the answer as their comment,
exactly as the web panel does, so the issue's agent wakes. The polling loop
now also takes callback_query updates.

Patch-Id: telegram-push
